  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "兒童與青少年文學",
    "sub_ename": "CHILDREN AND JUVENILE LITERATURE",
    "describe_ch": "此一課程主要為介紹兒童文學與青少年文學的定義、屬性、類別及寫作原理，並針對神話、寓言、童話、兒童與青少年小說、兒童與青少年戲劇等不同主題與文體，規畫研讀與專題，介紹其意義、特質、寫作原則，並以批判性思考進行作品的分析與小組討論。",
    "describe_eh": "This course aims to introduce students to different genres of children and juvenile literature. It will cover topics in mythology, fairy tales, plays, novels, science fiction, illustrator studies, writing styles and so on. An important and ambitious goal of this class is that students will enjoy reading children and juvenile novels as well as learn to understand themselves and the world around them better. Reading is delightful and over the course of this semester we will hopefully come to form a community of readers who are willing to share ideas, discuss and help one another understand and enhance critical thinking abilities. Active participation is essential to the success of this class.",
